# 7. CONTENT MODEL

Use normalized relational data in D1.

## Publication

Conceptual fields:

- id
- name
- slug
- description
- logo_media_id
- favicon_media_id
- default_cover_media_id
- locale
- timezone
- theme_config
- social_links
- seo_defaults
- created_at
- updated_at

## Author profile

- id
- auth_user_id
- display_name
- slug
- bio
- avatar_media_id
- website
- social_links
- created_at
- updated_at

`auth_user_id` must correspond to the external authenticated identity.

Do not duplicate passwords or authentication secrets.

## Post

- id
- author_id
- title
- slug
- dek/subtitle
- excerpt
- content_json
- content_html
- cover_media_id
- status
- visibility
- published_at
- scheduled_at (nullable, architecture-ready)
- reading_time_minutes
- canonical_url
- seo_title
- seo_description
- og_title
- og_description
- created_at
- updated_at
- deleted_at (nullable)

Suggested status:

- draft
- published
- archived

Visibility:

- public
- private

Keep state transitions explicit and validated.

## Post revision

- id
- post_id
- author_id
- content_json
- title
- dek
- excerpt
- seo fields
- cover_media_id
- created_at

Do not store unlimited gigantic duplicate payloads without reason.

Use a sane revision strategy.

## Category

- id
- name
- slug
- description
- created_at
- updated_at

## Tag

- id
- name
- slug
- created_at

## Post-category relation

- post_id
- category_id

## Post-tag relation

- post_id
- tag_id

## Media

Store Cloudinary references, not binary blobs.

Conceptual fields:

- id
- owner_auth_user_id
- cloudinary_public_id
- cloudinary_asset_id
- resource_type
- media_type
- secure_url
- width
- height
- duration
- format
- bytes
- alt_text
- caption
- credit
- folder
- created_at
- updated_at

Important:

The database is the application's source of truth for how the media asset is used.

Cloudinary remains the source of truth for the actual media asset.

## Comment

- id
- post_id
- author_name
- author_email (only when genuinely required; protect it)
- body
- status
- created_at
- updated_at

Suggested status:

- pending
- approved
- rejected
- spam

Do not expose private moderation data to public routes.

## Audit event

- id
- actor_auth_user_id
- action
- entity_type
- entity_id
- metadata_json
- created_at

Avoid storing secrets or sensitive tokens in audit metadata.

