# 10. AUTHENTICATION FLOW

Implement the actual current InsForge-auth flow, verified against the connected docs.

Conceptually:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Browser
    participant App as Next.js / Cloudflare
    participant Auth as InsForge Auth
    participant DB as D1

    Browser->>App: Open /studio
    App->>Auth: Resolve current authenticated session
    Auth-->>App: Verified identity / no session

    alt authenticated
        App->>DB: Load authorized content
        DB-->>App: Content
        App-->>Browser: Studio
    else unauthenticated
        App-->>Browser: Redirect / show auth
    end

    Browser->>App: Sign out
    App->>Auth: Invalidate/end session
    Auth-->>App: Success
    App-->>Browser: Signed-out state
```

Never implement a fake version of this flow.

The exact API/SDK behavior must come from current InsForge documentation/skills.

---

# 11. MEDIA UPLOAD FLOW

Cloudinary is responsible for media.

Target flow:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant UI as Studio
    participant App as Cloudflare / Worker
    participant C as Cloudinary
    participant DB as D1

    User->>UI: Select image/video
    UI->>App: Request upload authorization/signature
    App->>App: Verify authenticated user
    App-->>UI: Short-lived upload parameters

    UI->>C: Upload media
    C-->>UI: Asset result

    UI->>App: Save media metadata/reference
    App->>DB: Insert media row
    DB-->>App: Media ID
    App-->>UI: Media record
```

Requirements:

- never put Cloudinary API secret in browser code
- validate file type
- validate expected limits
- reject clearly dangerous/unacceptable content where practical
- generate deterministic folder conventions
- use user/publication scoping
- store Cloudinary public ID and asset metadata in D1
- support alt text
- support captions
- support credit/source
- provide upload progress
- provide clear failure states
- do not orphan database records when upload fails
- do not create database references before a successful Cloudinary asset creation unless transactional compensation is implemented

Recommended organization concept:

`cinderpress/{publication-id}/{media-type}/...`

The exact folder implementation must follow current Cloudinary guidance, including current folder mode behavior.

---

# 12. PUBLISHING FLOW

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Author
    participant Studio
    participant App
    participant DB
    participant Public

    Author->>Studio: Edit draft
    Studio->>App: Save
    App->>DB: Persist draft/revision

    Author->>Studio: Publish
    Studio->>App: Publish request
    App->>App: Verify auth + role + validation
    App->>DB: Set status=published
    App->>DB: Set published_at
    App-->>Studio: Published

    Public->>App: Request article
    App->>DB: Read published article
    DB-->>App: Article
    App-->>Public: Render article
```

On publish:

- validate title
- validate slug
- validate required content
- validate author
- validate cover media where required
- calculate/update reading time
- update canonical SEO metadata
- set publication timestamp if first published
- create revision if appropriate
- invalidate affected caches/tags
- update search index
- return a clear result

Do not allow drafts to leak onto public pages.

